  "result": "I found and fixed one cause of the odd ordering in `--help`, but I'm not certain it's the one you meant, since you didn't say what order you saw.\n\n**What changed:** In `join_options` (`src/click/formatting.py:319`), the names for a single option were sorted by prefix length in reverse. A `-v` / `--verbose` option therefore printed as `--verbose, -v` instead of `-v, --verbose`. I removed `reverse=True`.\n\n**Not touched:** The order of the options themselves in the list comes from `Command.get_params` and `format_options`, and that code is fine. The `reversed(decorator_params)` in `decorators.py` is intentional, because decorators apply bottom-up.\n\n**Tests:** The full suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). No test covers this ordering, so I didn't add one.\n\nIf the odd order you saw was between different options rather than within one option's names, tell me what you saw and I'll look again.",
